<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n110776" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φῐβάλεως</span></b> 
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">[ᾰ]</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ω</span>, ἡ, a kind of <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>early fig,</i> found in Com. in pl., nom.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φιβάλεῳ </span>(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φιβαλέοι</span> codd.<i><span class="en">
				Ath.
			</span></i>) <i><span class="en">
				Telecl.
				5
			</span></i>: gen., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῶν φιβάλεων συκων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pherecr.
					80
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φιβάλεων</span> alone, <i><span class="en">
				Hermipp.
				51
			</span></i>: acc., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φιβάλεως ἰσχάδας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ar.
					<u>Ach.</u>
					802
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φιβάλεως</span> alone, <i><span class="en">
				Apolloph.
				5
			</span></i>.—Sch.<i><span class="en">
				Ar.
			</span></i> l.c. has <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γένος συκῆς ἡ
			φίβαλις</span> (taking <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φιβάλεως</span>
			as gen. sg.) and explains as the name for a district in Megaris or
			Attica; <i><span class="en">
				<u>EM</u>
				793.26
			</span></i> has <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φιβάλεως: γένος συκῆς: λέγουσι
				δὲ οὕτω καὶ τὰς μιρρίνας.</span>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>a lean, dried-up person,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Telecl.
			</span></i> l. c., Sch.<i><span class="en">
				Ar.
			</span></i> l. c., <i><span class="en">
				Suid.
			</span></i></div>
